{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>To hear</b> — as in the way of: \"and Elohim heard their groaning\" (Exodus 2:24), on account of the prisoner. He said <b>to those about to die</b> [לפתח ובני תמותה] — who are prepared for slaughter and death, like <b>תקומה תרומה</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {0 "The phrase 'he said to those about to die' appears to cite or allude to a verse; the comparison to 'תקומה תרומה' is obscure and rendered literally without resolution."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:52.542705923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}